WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.422 --> 00:00:03.182
Companies are being overwhelmed by data.

00:00:03.182 --> 00:00:06.442
Suddenly they have all sorts of
information about their customers,

00:00:06.442 --> 00:00:08.644
their employees, about financial markets.

00:00:08.644 --> 00:00:09.956
But what are you going to do with that?

00:00:09.956 --> 00:00:11.698
How do you harvest that data and

00:00:11.698 --> 00:00:15.384
put it to work for your company so
that you make better decisions?

00:00:15.384 --> 00:00:19.016
[MUSIC]

00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:22.042
There are a lot of executives out
there who know they have this data.

00:00:22.042 --> 00:00:25.427
They have some analytical ability,
but they're not experts on it.

00:00:25.427 --> 00:00:29.696
And we want to help them think about
the processes, the procedures, and

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.988
the tools out there.

00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:33.378
How do I get the right information and

00:00:33.378 --> 00:00:38.313
put it to use in a way that's going to be
valuable, it's going to be actionable,

00:00:38.313 --> 00:00:41.106
it's going to make
the company work better?

00:00:41.106 --> 00:00:44.265
&gt;&gt; I wanted to learn more about big data,

00:00:44.265 --> 00:00:47.934
how to make decisions
with help of big data.

00:00:47.934 --> 00:00:52.458
&gt;&gt; This program provides you with
deep insights on how you can use

00:00:52.458 --> 00:00:56.548
big data at the heart of your
business strategies to make

00:00:56.548 --> 00:00:59.954
better management
decisions on many fronts.

00:00:59.954 --> 00:01:03.199
&gt;&gt; The role of the executive
has never been more important.

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:07.692
As we fill up the ranks of firms and
engineering staffs with people who

00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:11.179
are really amazing at writing
great computer code and

00:01:11.179 --> 00:01:13.891
making predictions, at using the data,

00:01:13.891 --> 00:01:18.406
it becomes ever more important to
have powerful leaders in the room.

00:01:18.406 --> 00:01:21.659
Who can ask, are we really even
trying to predict the right thing?

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:24.183
Are we going after the right metric?

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:26.571
&gt;&gt; The ideal participant for Big Data,

00:01:26.571 --> 00:01:30.737
Strategic Decisions Analysis to Action,
is a senior manager.

00:01:30.737 --> 00:01:34.840
They want to know, how do I interface with
my data scientists, my market analysts?

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.217
How do I take the data and
how do I make my company run better?

00:01:39.217 --> 00:01:41.401
&gt;&gt; As opposed to be being
down in the details,

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.415
we have an amazing team that does that.

00:01:43.415 --> 00:01:46.891
But as a leader I really wanted to
understand how can that aid with my

00:01:46.891 --> 00:01:47.891
decision making.

00:01:47.891 --> 00:01:52.159
&gt;&gt; If those executives can compliment
those skills they already have with

00:01:52.159 --> 00:01:56.922
knowledge of what big data can do for
that business, that's an opportunity for

00:01:56.922 --> 00:02:01.428
those people to take their careers and
their businesses to the next level.

00:02:01.428 --> 00:02:03.955
Throughout the week you will spend time

00:02:03.955 --> 00:02:08.254
working on a team to try to solve
an actual problem using real data.

00:02:08.254 --> 00:02:10.619
&gt;&gt; The real data challenge is,
it's very intense.

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:12.337
There is a lot of interaction.

00:02:12.337 --> 00:02:15.485
&gt;&gt; We had very interesting guest speakers.

00:02:15.485 --> 00:02:20.163
&gt;&gt; People who actually employ this big
data techniques in their companies.

00:02:20.163 --> 00:02:22.388
&gt;&gt; How they evolved with time.

00:02:22.388 --> 00:02:26.526
How they used the big data to
improve their product offering.

00:02:26.526 --> 00:02:30.056
&gt;&gt; This is where innovation happens,
and that is special here.

00:02:30.056 --> 00:02:31.312
And that's something you feel.

00:02:31.312 --> 00:02:35.937
&gt;&gt; It's really the seasoned manager who
